              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఎడమ (eḍama) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil iṭam and Kannada eḍa, \"left side\" (DEDR 449). DEDR compares the Indo-Aryan words for \"left\" in CDIAL 5539, such as Hindi ḍāwā, which CDIAL itself calls non-Aryan, perhaps from Dravidian."
